'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_hub75_morphMotion.spin2
''   Purpose.... Board test of time-based motion: move duration at two frame rates, a long frame, mid-move commands, setters
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 12 Oct 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Task 163, phase 2 (ported to the task 166 renderer): proves the animate(nowMs) contract on the quad.

  The probe is the screen buffer itself. The test segment is segment A of a digit 1 pixel thick and 31 long, drawn
  with the edge profile through a test ramp whose red byte IS the level (no gamma), so the sum of the red bytes of
  A's row / 255 is the segment's lit amount, in pixels. litTenths() reads those bytes back through
  screenUtils.pixelAddressAtRC(); it never asks the segment. Time comes from isp_hub75_morphTime; the move-duration
  checks also read getct() themselves, an independent count of the same interval.

  Expected lit amounts are worked out from the profile, not from the code: with the edge profile the head runs
  h = p x (L + 1) pixels over the move (p the share done), and the lit amount turning on is
      h^2 / 2  (h <= 1),   h - 1/2  (1 <= h <= L),   L - (L + 1 - h)^2 / 2  (h >= L)
  and turning off, L minus that. Amounts are compared in tenths of a pixel.

  Sections:
    1. a 300 ms move takes 300 ms, never less and at most one frame more, at the natural (commit-paced) frame
       rate and at a slower rate forced by a waitms() in every frame
    2. a frame forced long (LONG_FRAME_MS) during a 3 s move: the next frame draws the position for the time that
       has passed (a jump of many pixels), and the frame-rate meter's figure drops
    3. a command arriving mid-move snaps the move in flight to its end, then starts the new move
    4. smoothstep easing puts the segment where 3p^2 - 2p^3 says (expected amounts worked out by hand below)
    5. the group setters refuse out-of-range values with an error code and change nothing (R-10.2)

  Log lines this program adds to the harness's lines (same field style):
    MOVE      <name>  move_ms=<n>  measured_ms=<n>  ticks_ms=<n>  frames=<n>  max_frame_ms=<n>
    LONGFRAME lit_before_x10=<n>  expected_before_x10=<n>  lit_after_x10=<n>  expected_after_x10=<n>  elapsed_after_ms=<n>  fps_before_x100=<n>  fps_after_x100=<n>
}

CON ' ---- Timing ----

  CLK_FREQ = 335_000_000                                        ' system freq as a constant
  _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ                                           ' set system clock

CON ' ---- Test segment and moves ----

  DIGIT_ROW = 40                                                ' the test digit; its segment A is row 40 ...
  DIGIT_COLUMN = 7                                              ' ... columns 8 to 38
  SEG_ROW = DIGIT_ROW
  SEG_COLUMN = DIGIT_COLUMN + 1
  SEG_LENGTH = 31                                               ' 31 pixels: the head runs 32 pixels over a move
  SEG_THICKNESS = 1
  SLOT_A = 6                                                    ' segment A's slot in the digit
  MASK_BYTES = 64                                               ' the figure's masks at T1 L31: 31 + 3 + 4 + 1 bytes
  EDGE_TAIL_X256 = 256                                          ' the edge profile: a 1-pixel tail
  TENTHS = 10                                                   ' lit amounts are compared in tenths of a pixel
  FULL_TENTHS = SEG_LENGTH * TENTHS
  MOVE_MS = 300                                                 ' the plan's verify case
  HALF_MOVE_MS = MOVE_MS / 2
  QUARTER_MOVE_MS = MOVE_MS / 4
  THREE_QUARTER_MOVE_MS = MOVE_MS - QUARTER_MOVE_MS
  SLOW_FRAME_EXTRA_MS = 40                                      ' added to every frame of the slow run: about 18 frames/s instead of 71
  NO_EXTRA_MS = 0
  TIMING_SLACK_MS = 1                                           ' getct and the time base floor the same interval to whole ms separately
  ONE_MS = 1                                                    ' the smallest step past a limit
  X100 = 100                                                    ' onTenths() works in hundredths of a pixel ...
  HALF_X100 = X100 / 2                                          ' ... half a pixel
  SQUARE_X100_TO_TENTHS = 2 * X100 * X100 / TENTHS              ' (h x 100)^2 / this = h^2 / 2 in tenths
  ONE_PIXEL = 1
  HALF_OFF_TENTHS = 155                                         ' p = 0.5 turning off: h = 16, on amount 15.5, off = 31 - 15.5

CON ' ---- Long frame ----

  LONG_MOVE_MS = 3000                                           ' about 94 ms per pixel: the jump is easy to see
  LEAD_IN_MS = 2100                                             ' natural idle frames first: at least one whole meter window at the natural rate
  BEFORE_LONG_MS = 500                                          ' natural frames of the move before the long frame
  LONG_FRAME_MS = 1500                                          ' longer than the meter's window, so the update() after it closes the window that holds it
  MIN_SKIP_TENTHS = 100                                         ' the long frame must advance at least 10 pixels (one frame advances under 1)
  AMOUNT_TOLERANCE_TENTHS = 2                                   ' expected amount against the code's Q15 truncation and per-column rounding
  DROP_DIVISOR = 2                                              ' after the long frame the meter must read under half its natural figure

CON ' ---- Injected times and easing ----

  INJECT_BASE_MS = 100_000                                      ' injected times start here (any value: only differences count)
  INJECT_GAP_MS = 10_000                                        ' each injected move starts this far after the previous one
  ' smoothstep, worked out by hand: p_s = 3p^2 - 2p^3, h = 32 p_s, on amount h - 1/2
  SMOOTH_TENTHS_AT_QUARTER = 45                                 ' p = 0.25: p_s = 0.15625, h = 5.0, amount 4.5
  SMOOTH_TENTHS_AT_3_QUARTERS = 265                         ' p = 0.75: p_s = 0.84375, h = 27.0, amount 26.5
  LINEAR_TENTHS_AT_QUARTER = 75                                 ' p = 0.25 linear: h = 8.0, amount 7.5 (smoothstep must differ from this)

CON ' ---- Group under test ----

  GROUP_ROW = 60
  GROUP_COLUMN = 100
  GROUP_AREA_WIDTH = 17                                         ' the area that fits segment length 15 at stroke 1: a digit 17 x 33
  GROUP_AREA_HEIGHT = 33
  GROUP_SEG_LENGTH = 15                                         ' segment A: 15 pixels
  GROUP_START_VALUE = 0                                         ' 0 -> 1: segment A snakes off left to right
  GROUP_A_COLUMN = GROUP_COLUMN + 1                             ' segment A starts one pixel right of the digit's left edge
  ' edge profile, p = 0.25 smoothstep: h = 16 x 0.15625 = 2.5; column 0 is dark, column 1 keeps 1/8 lit: 14 lit pixels
  ' (linear would give h = 4: columns 0-2 dark, 12 lit)
  GROUP_LIT_AT_QUARTER = 14
  HOLD_MS = 200
  UNKNOWN_EASING_STYLE = 99                                     ' no easing style has this value
  REPEAT_ASKS = 3                                               ' a pure query asked this many times gives one answer

OBJ

    color       : "isp_hub75_color"
    display     : "isp_hub75_display"
    pixels      : "isp_hub75_screenUtils"
    hub75Bffrs  : "isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess"
    utils       : "test_hub75_morphUtils"
    timeBase    : "isp_hub75_morphTime"
    dig         : "isp_hub75_morph7seg"
    seg         : "isp_hub75_morphSegment"                      ' command constants only
    group       : "isp_hub75_morphCounters"
    morphStatus : "isp_hub75_morphStatus"
    morphMask   : "isp_hub75_morphMask"
    morphColor  : "isp_hub75_morphColor"

VAR

    long    chainIndex
    long    maxRows
    long    maxColumns
    long    linearRamp[morphColor.RAMP_LEVELS]
    byte    mask[MASK_BYTES]

PUB go() | level
'' Run the motion test: start the display, run each section, finish.
''

    utils.beginSuite(@"morphMotion time-based motion")
    chainIndex := hub75Bffrs.indexForHub75ChainId(hub75Bffrs.HUB75_ADAPTER_1)
    display.start(display.HUB75_ADAPTER_1)
    maxColumns := hub75Bffrs.maxDisplayColumns(chainIndex)
    maxRows := hub75Bffrs.maxDisplayRows(chainIndex)
    display.clearScreen()
    display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
    timeBase.reset()

    ' the probe's ramp: red byte = level, through the driver's own packing
    repeat level from 0 to morphColor.RAMP_MAX
        linearRamp[level] := pixels.packedCorrectedRgb(chainIndex, level, 0, 0)
    morphMask.buildFigure(@mask, MASK_BYTES, SEG_THICKNESS, SEG_LENGTH, SEG_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    dig.initialize(chainIndex, maxRows, maxColumns)
    dig.placeDigit(DIGIT_ROW, DIGIT_COLUMN, SEG_LENGTH, SEG_THICKNESS, dig.DIGIT_HIDDEN, @mask, @linearRamp, EDGE_TAIL_X256)
    dig.animate(timeBase.update())
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"probe: the placed segment reads all dark", 0)

    checkMoveTiming(@"natural frame rate, turning on", NO_EXTRA_MS, seg.CMD_TURN_ON | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT, FULL_TENTHS)
    checkMoveTiming(@"slow frame rate, turning off", SLOW_FRAME_EXTRA_MS, seg.CMD_TURN_OFF | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT, 0)
    checkLongFrame()
    checkSnap()
    checkEasing()
    checkGroupSetters()

    utils.finish()


PRI checkMoveTiming(pName, extraMs, command, endTenths) | nowMs, startMs, prevMs, maxFrameMs, frameCount, startTick, endTick, measuredMs, tickMs
    ' run a MOVE_MS move in a real frame loop (update, animate, commit) and time it from the frame that stamps its start
    ' to the frame that completes it

    dig.setMotion(MOVE_MS, timeBase.EASE_LINEAR)
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, command)
    nowMs := timeBase.update()
    startTick := getct()
    startMs := nowMs
    prevMs := nowMs
    endTick := startTick
    maxFrameMs := 0
    frameCount := 0
    dig.animate(nowMs)                                          ' stamps the move's start at startMs
    repeat until dig.isAnimationComplete()
        display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
        if extraMs > 0
            waitms(extraMs)
        nowMs := timeBase.update()
        endTick := getct()
        maxFrameMs := maxFrameMs #> (nowMs - prevMs)
        prevMs := nowMs
        frameCount++
        dig.animate(nowMs)
    display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
    measuredMs := nowMs - startMs
    tickMs := muldiv64(endTick - startTick, timeBase.MS_PER_SECOND, clkfreq)
    debug("MOVE      ", zstr_(pName), "  move_ms=", udec_(MOVE_MS), "  measured_ms=", sdec_(measuredMs), "  ticks_ms=", udec_(tickMs), "  frames=", udec_(frameCount), "  max_frame_ms=", sdec_(maxFrameMs))

    utils.checkEqual(measuredMs >= MOVE_MS, @"the move never ends before its duration", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(measuredMs <= MOVE_MS + maxFrameMs, @"the move ends at most one frame after its duration", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(abs (tickMs - measuredMs) <= TIMING_SLACK_MS, @"getct agrees with the time base on the move's length", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"the segment ends on its target (lit tenths)", endTenths)


PRI checkLongFrame() | nowMs, leadStartMs, startMs, litBefore, litAfter, elapsedBefore, elapsedAfter, expectedBefore, expectedAfter, fpsBeforeX100, fpsAfterX100
    ' natural frames, then a 3 s move whose middle holds one frame of LONG_FRAME_MS

    dig.setMotion(LONG_MOVE_MS, timeBase.EASE_LINEAR)
    nowMs := timeBase.update()
    leadStartMs := nowMs
    repeat while nowMs - leadStartMs < LEAD_IN_MS
        display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
        nowMs := timeBase.update()
    fpsBeforeX100 := timeBase.framesPerSecondX100()

    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_ON | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    nowMs := timeBase.update()
    startMs := nowMs
    dig.animate(nowMs)
    repeat while nowMs - startMs < BEFORE_LONG_MS
        display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
        nowMs := timeBase.update()
        dig.animate(nowMs)
    litBefore := litTenths()
    elapsedBefore := nowMs - startMs

    display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
    waitms(LONG_FRAME_MS)                                       ' the forced long frame
    nowMs := timeBase.update()
    dig.animate(nowMs)
    litAfter := litTenths()
    elapsedAfter := nowMs - startMs
    fpsAfterX100 := timeBase.framesPerSecondX100()

    ' the amount for an elapsed time, from the exact ratio (not the code's arithmetic)
    expectedBefore := onTenths(elapsedBefore, LONG_MOVE_MS)
    expectedAfter := onTenths(elapsedAfter, LONG_MOVE_MS)
    debug("LONGFRAME lit_before_x10=", udec_(litBefore), "  expected_before_x10=", udec_(expectedBefore), "  lit_after_x10=", udec_(litAfter), "  expected_after_x10=", udec_(expectedAfter), "  elapsed_after_ms=", sdec_(elapsedAfter), "  fps_before_x100=", udec_(fpsBeforeX100), "  fps_after_x100=", udec_(fpsAfterX100))

    utils.checkEqual(abs (litBefore - expectedBefore) <= AMOUNT_TOLERANCE_TENTHS, @"natural frames: the drawn amount follows the time", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(abs (litAfter - expectedAfter) <= AMOUNT_TOLERANCE_TENTHS, @"after the long frame: the drawn amount is the one for the time passed", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(litAfter - litBefore >= MIN_SKIP_TENTHS, @"the long frame skips ahead many pixels, it does not slow the move", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(fpsAfterX100 < fpsBeforeX100 / DROP_DIVISOR, @"the frame-rate meter reports the drop", TRUE)

    repeat until dig.isAnimationComplete()
        display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
        dig.animate(timeBase.update())
    display.commitScreenToPanelSet()
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"the long move ends fully on", FULL_TENTHS)


PRI checkSnap() | injectMs
    ' injected times: a command that arrives mid-move, opposite and same-direction

    dig.setMotion(MOVE_MS, timeBase.EASE_LINEAR)
    injectMs := INJECT_BASE_MS

    ' the segment is on: turning it off left to right, half way
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_OFF | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    dig.animate(injectMs)
    dig.animate(injectMs + HALF_MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"mid-move: half of the segment has turned off (15.5 px lit)", HALF_OFF_TENTHS)

    ' the opposite command: the off move snaps to its end (dark), then the on move starts from nothing lit
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_ON | seg.CMD_RT_TO_LT)
    injectMs += INJECT_GAP_MS
    dig.animate(injectMs)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"opposite command mid-move: snapped to off, the new move starts dark", 0)
    utils.checkEqual(dig.isAnimationComplete(), @"opposite command mid-move: the new move is running", FALSE)
    dig.animate(injectMs + MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"opposite command mid-move: the digit ends on the last command's target", FULL_TENTHS)

    ' the same command again mid-move: the move snaps to its end, and the repeat has nothing left to do
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_OFF | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    injectMs += INJECT_GAP_MS
    dig.animate(injectMs)
    dig.animate(injectMs + HALF_MOVE_MS)
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_OFF | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    dig.animate(injectMs + HALF_MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"same command mid-move: snapped to its end (off)", 0)
    utils.checkEqual(dig.isAnimationComplete(), @"same command mid-move: nothing left to move", TRUE)


PRI checkEasing() | injectMs
    ' injected times: smoothstep at a quarter and three quarters of the move

    dig.setMotion(MOVE_MS, timeBase.EASE_SMOOTH)
    injectMs := INJECT_BASE_MS
    dig.commandSegment(SLOT_A, seg.CMD_TURN_ON | seg.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    dig.animate(injectMs)
    dig.animate(injectMs + QUARTER_MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"smoothstep at a quarter of the move", SMOOTH_TENTHS_AT_QUARTER)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths() <> LINEAR_TENTHS_AT_QUARTER, @"smoothstep differs from linear at a quarter", TRUE)
    dig.animate(injectMs + THREE_QUARTER_MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"smoothstep at three quarters of the move", SMOOTH_TENTHS_AT_3_QUARTERS)
    dig.animate(injectMs + MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(litTenths(), @"smoothstep ends fully on", FULL_TENTHS)
    dig.setMotion(MOVE_MS, timeBase.EASE_LINEAR)


PRI checkGroupSetters() | injectMs, bAllComplete
    ' the group's setters: accepted values, refused values, then the 0 -> 1 transition shows nothing changed

    group.setProfile(timeBase.PROFILE_EDGE)
    group.setThickness(SEG_THICKNESS)
    group.placeGroup(hub75Bffrs.HUB75_ADAPTER_1, GROUP_COLUMN, GROUP_ROW, GROUP_AREA_WIDTH, GROUP_AREA_HEIGHT, group.GRP_UP_COUNTER, group.LAYOUT_1_DIGIT, group.ROT_0, color.cGreen, GROUP_START_VALUE)
    group.animate(INJECT_BASE_MS)                               ' the placed digit grows in ...
    group.animate(INJECT_BASE_MS + timeBase.DEFAULT_MOVE_MS)     ' ... and rests
    utils.checkEqual(groupALit(), @"probe: digit 0 shows segment A fully lit", GROUP_SEG_LENGTH)

    utils.checkEqual(group.setMoveDuration(MOVE_MS), @"setMoveDuration accepts 300 ms", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setMoveDuration(group.MIN_MOVE_MS - ONE_MS), @"setMoveDuration refuses 0 ms", morphStatus.E_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setMoveDuration(group.MAX_TIME_MS + ONE_MS), @"setMoveDuration refuses one ms over the limit", morphStatus.E_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setHoldDuration(HOLD_MS), @"setHoldDuration accepts 200 ms", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setHoldDuration(group.MIN_HOLD_MS - ONE_MS), @"setHoldDuration refuses -1 ms", morphStatus.E_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setHoldDuration(group.MAX_TIME_MS + ONE_MS), @"setHoldDuration refuses one ms over the limit", morphStatus.E_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setEasing(timeBase.EASE_SMOOTH), @"setEasing accepts smoothstep", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(group.setEasing(UNKNOWN_EASING_STYLE), @"setEasing refuses an unknown style", morphStatus.E_UNKNOWN_EASING)

    ' the 0 -> 1 transition runs with what was accepted: 300 ms, smoothstep, a 200 ms hold
    injectMs := INJECT_BASE_MS + INJECT_GAP_MS
    group.nextTimeCycle()
    group.animate(injectMs)
    group.animate(injectMs + QUARTER_MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(groupALit(), @"refused easing left smoothstep in place (lit pixels at a quarter)", GROUP_LIT_AT_QUARTER)
    group.animate(injectMs + MOVE_MS - ONE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(group.isAnimationComplete(), @"refused durations left 300 ms in place: still moving at 299 ms", FALSE)
    group.animate(injectMs + MOVE_MS)
    utils.checkEqual(group.isAnimationComplete(), @"refused durations left 300 ms in place: complete at 300 ms", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(groupALit(), @"the group's transition ends on its target (A dark)", 0)
    bAllComplete := TRUE
    repeat REPEAT_ASKS
        if group.isAnimationComplete() == FALSE
            bAllComplete := FALSE
    utils.checkEqual(bAllComplete, @"isAnimationComplete is a pure query: asked 3 times, TRUE each time", TRUE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.isHoldComplete(injectMs + MOVE_MS + HOLD_MS - ONE_MS), @"refused holds left 200 ms in place: holding at 199 ms", FALSE)
    utils.checkEqual(group.isHoldComplete(injectMs + MOVE_MS + HOLD_MS), @"refused holds left 200 ms in place: hold over at 200 ms", TRUE)


PRI onTenths(elapsedMs, moveMs) : amountTenths | headX100
    ' the lit amount turning on, in tenths of a pixel, after elapsedMs of a linear moveMs move (see the notes above)

    headX100 := muldiv64(elapsedMs <# moveMs, (SEG_LENGTH + ONE_PIXEL) * X100, moveMs)
    if headX100 <= X100
        amountTenths := headX100 * headX100 / SQUARE_X100_TO_TENTHS
    elseif headX100 <= SEG_LENGTH * X100
        amountTenths := (headX100 - HALF_X100) / (X100 / TENTHS)
    else
        amountTenths := FULL_TENTHS - ((SEG_LENGTH + ONE_PIXEL) * X100 - headX100) * ((SEG_LENGTH + ONE_PIXEL) * X100 - headX100) / SQUARE_X100_TO_TENTHS


PRI litTenths() : amountTenths | column, pPixel, total
    ' the test segment's lit amount, in tenths of a pixel: the red bytes of its row (the level, through the linear ramp)

    total := 0
    column := SEG_COLUMN
    repeat SEG_LENGTH
        pPixel := pixels.pixelAddressAtRC(chainIndex, SEG_ROW, column++)
        if pPixel <> hub75Bffrs.NO_PIXEL
            total += BYTE[pPixel]
    amountTenths := (total * TENTHS + morphColor.RAMP_MAX / (TENTHS / TENTHS + ONE_PIXEL)) / morphColor.RAMP_MAX


PRI groupALit() : nLit
    ' lit pixels of the group's segment A

    nLit := litCount(GROUP_ROW, GROUP_A_COLUMN, GROUP_SEG_LENGTH)


PRI litCount(row, firstColumn, nColumns) : nLit | column, pPixel, byteIdx, nBytes, bLit
    ' count the pixels of a row run whose screen-buffer bytes are not all zero (black is all zero)

    nLit := 0
    nBytes := hub75Bffrs.bytesPerColor(chainIndex)
    column := firstColumn
    repeat nColumns
        pPixel := pixels.pixelAddressAtRC(chainIndex, row, column)
        if pPixel <> hub75Bffrs.NO_PIXEL
            bLit := FALSE
            byteIdx := 0
            repeat nBytes
                if BYTE[pPixel][byteIdx] <> 0
                    bLit := TRUE
                byteIdx++
            if bLit
                nLit++
        column++


CON ' ---- License ----

